WEBVTT

00:12.320 --> 00:14.280
I'm parched...

00:14.280 --> 00:16.380
Give me water...

00:19.930 --> 00:22.670
There are essential pillars.

00:23.250 --> 00:27.010
Seventy and two, they cross
the foundation of the stars.

00:27.800 --> 00:30.250
When they are lost,

00:30.810 --> 00:34.560
their axes become strained,
and the stars disintegrate.

00:35.820 --> 00:40.140
Seventy and two gods protect
the essential pillars.

00:40.720 --> 00:44.250
They are like an illusion.

02:08.540 --> 02:11.980
I'll Find It!

02:12.550 --> 02:15.860
It's tough not having anything
to block the sunlight.

02:16.210 --> 02:19.550
I wanted to tan at the beach,
not get sunburned in the desert.

02:19.550 --> 02:21.780
My skin is ruined.

02:22.210 --> 02:26.040
I'm so pale, my skin turns
bright red and swells up.

02:26.370 --> 02:28.340
You're all so delicate.

02:28.340 --> 02:29.790
It doesn't bother me.

02:29.790 --> 02:32.850
Yeah, I didn't think so,

02:32.850 --> 02:36.080
but that doesn't explain
why your skin is so nice.

02:36.080 --> 02:38.150
Are you sure you're not secretly
taking care of your skin?

02:38.150 --> 02:40.090
I've never done anything like that.

02:40.090 --> 02:41.550
I'm so jealous.

02:42.320 --> 02:47.430
At this rate, we're all going
to collapse from dehydration.

02:47.430 --> 02:49.310
Levi-tan, make some
water with your magic.

02:49.310 --> 02:50.020
What?

02:50.020 --> 02:52.080
Could I get some, too, please?

02:52.080 --> 02:54.150
Me, too, Levi-tan.

02:54.430 --> 02:57.190
When did I become Levi-tan?

02:57.190 --> 02:58.400
Who cares?

02:58.400 --> 03:00.010
It's cute.

03:00.010 --> 03:02.310
C-Cute...

03:02.310 --> 03:04.720
Forget about that. Magic, magic.

03:08.260 --> 03:09.290
Water...

03:10.250 --> 03:11.920
You can use a stick you
picked up off the ground.

03:11.920 --> 03:13.630
What? Oh...

03:17.870 --> 03:20.690
It's all right. I'm a water user.

03:21.140 --> 03:23.390
Water, come to me.

03:31.330 --> 03:32.060
There it is.

03:32.290 --> 03:33.300
What? Where?

03:33.300 --> 03:34.580
Where is it?

03:34.580 --> 03:35.930
Is that it?

03:52.060 --> 03:53.900
We were so close.

03:53.900 --> 03:54.960
Don't worry about it.

03:54.960 --> 03:56.340
Levi-tan, one more time.

03:56.630 --> 03:57.440
What?

03:58.420 --> 04:00.760
Water, come to me again.

04:02.260 --> 04:02.930
There it is.

04:03.180 --> 04:04.360
Where?

04:04.360 --> 04:05.620
Where is it?

04:06.100 --> 04:06.990
Is that it?

04:14.810 --> 04:17.270
I don't think I can take any more.

04:17.500 --> 04:18.840
Oh, come on.

04:18.840 --> 04:21.190
Can't you do anything without your spear?

04:21.190 --> 04:23.030
Not that you can do anything
even when you have it.

04:30.040 --> 04:33.190
I know this is a desert, but it's huge.

04:33.190 --> 04:34.540
It's enormous.

04:34.890 --> 04:37.540
How far are we supposed to go?

04:37.860 --> 04:39.400
Why don't we go home?

04:39.400 --> 04:42.550
I'm thirsty and I'm hungry!

04:42.550 --> 04:46.650
I'm sick of this! I'm not walking any more!

04:46.650 --> 04:48.300
Is dinner ready yet?!

04:48.690 --> 04:50.740
Dinner, dinner, dinner!

04:50.740 --> 04:52.380
You seem to have plenty of energy.

04:56.560 --> 04:59.400
I'm rather hungry, too.

04:59.400 --> 05:01.720
And the sun's starting to set.

05:01.720 --> 05:04.450
We should stop and start
preparing for dinner.

05:04.450 --> 05:05.820
Do it, then!

05:05.820 --> 05:08.160
I'm not moving from this spot!

05:08.470 --> 05:09.660
A snake.

05:10.400 --> 05:11.700
She moved.

05:11.700 --> 05:14.130
Wh-Wh-Where is it?!

05:14.130 --> 05:15.390
Hurry up and kill it!

05:16.940 --> 05:19.790
Well, it's a valuable source of food.

05:19.790 --> 05:21.920
Oh, right. We can eat it.

05:22.710 --> 05:23.960
Thanks for the food.

05:29.180 --> 05:31.010
Don't you know how to hold back?

05:31.010 --> 05:32.100
Sorry.

05:32.420 --> 05:35.650
Our precious food...

05:35.650 --> 05:38.060
Do you think there's still something
around here somewhere?

06:17.160 --> 06:17.850
Well, then.

06:18.110 --> 06:20.060
Thanks for the food!

06:20.460 --> 06:21.860
What? Just like that?

06:21.860 --> 06:22.880
Huh?

06:22.880 --> 06:24.140
You're just going to cook it?

06:24.140 --> 06:25.210
You're kidding, right?

06:25.210 --> 06:28.440
Aren't you going to flambé it or
put some béchamel sauce on it?

06:30.000 --> 06:31.940
If you don't hurry, there won't be any left.

06:31.940 --> 06:33.480
B-But...

06:33.480 --> 06:35.170
If you're not going to eat,
I'll have some more.

06:35.170 --> 06:36.890
Me, too.

06:36.890 --> 06:39.500
What? I-Is it good?

06:40.020 --> 06:41.830
It doesn't really taste like anything.

06:42.100 --> 06:44.090
It really has no flavor.

06:44.090 --> 06:45.380
Oh, no...

06:46.830 --> 06:47.910
What should I do?

06:57.920 --> 07:00.080
It's pretty cold once the sun goes down.

07:00.080 --> 07:01.810
Let's rest.

07:01.810 --> 07:03.910
I'm just getting hungry staying awake.

07:03.910 --> 07:05.240
I'm going to sleep, too.

07:05.240 --> 07:06.990
Where are we going to sleep tonight?

07:06.990 --> 07:07.910
Where's our inn?

07:07.910 --> 07:09.310
We're camping out here.

07:09.310 --> 07:12.630
Camping out? Camping out...

07:12.630 --> 07:13.570
We're sleeping outdoors?!

07:13.920 --> 07:15.220
Yeah, pretty much.

07:15.220 --> 07:16.660
What?!

07:17.050 --> 07:20.160
I think it's best if we start
moving before the sun comes up,

07:20.160 --> 07:21.420
so let's go to sleep now.

07:21.700 --> 07:23.570
Good night, then.

07:23.570 --> 07:26.680
Good night. Pleasant dreams.

07:26.680 --> 07:28.310
Huh? What?

07:28.310 --> 07:32.030
Wait, everyone! I've never
slept outdoors before!

07:32.030 --> 07:33.560
Wake up, wake up!

07:33.560 --> 07:36.720
Shut up. We have to wake
up early tomorrow.

07:38.230 --> 07:39.890
No, no!

07:39.890 --> 07:41.520
Wake up, wake up!

07:41.520 --> 07:43.040
I can't sleep!

07:43.040 --> 07:45.630
Let's look for an inn!

08:34.810 --> 08:35.950
I found it.

08:38.540 --> 08:41.200
Is it morning or evening?

08:43.110 --> 08:45.960
Huh? Is something wrong, Leviatan?

08:47.200 --> 08:49.290
I found my spear.

08:49.290 --> 08:51.140
What? Really?!

08:51.140 --> 08:53.320
Where, where, where?

08:53.320 --> 08:54.200
Where is it?

08:54.200 --> 08:55.470
In my dream.

08:55.690 --> 08:56.790
What?

08:56.790 --> 08:59.220
You found it where?
Do you want us to say something?

09:00.540 --> 09:02.980
I'm walking through some ruins.

09:03.720 --> 09:06.480
There's an area like an altar,

09:06.810 --> 09:09.300
and my spear is stuck in it.

09:09.900 --> 09:11.870
I know it was my spear.

09:13.050 --> 09:15.870
Another dream?

09:15.870 --> 09:17.220
Yes...

09:17.220 --> 09:18.860
Did you recognize the place?

09:18.860 --> 09:19.990
I don't know.

09:22.040 --> 09:23.890
Some ruins, huh?

09:23.890 --> 09:26.040
Is there anywhere like that?

09:26.040 --> 09:29.320
When I was a kid, I went to a
spring with some ruins once.

09:29.320 --> 09:31.500
But it wasn't in a desert,
so that can't be it, right?

09:31.850 --> 09:36.760
The place across the Fulmic River from
town and beyond the meadow?

09:36.760 --> 09:38.270
Yeah, there.

09:39.140 --> 09:42.260
Isn't that the beautiful place with
the stone columns in the spring?

09:42.620 --> 09:45.620
That's the place I went for my first adventure.

09:45.620 --> 09:46.480
Yeah, that's it.

09:46.910 --> 09:50.650
I went there on my first journey alone, too.

09:50.960 --> 09:53.290
You're all talking about the same place.

09:53.290 --> 09:54.400
What's it like?

09:54.400 --> 09:55.900
It's surrounded by vegetation.

09:56.410 --> 09:59.650
There's a spring in the
middle of some stone ruins,

09:59.650 --> 10:01.910
and there are floating
islands in the sky above it.

10:02.430 --> 10:05.910
Water flows from there into
the spring on the ground.

10:05.910 --> 10:10.180
The spray fills the entire
spring with negative ions,

10:10.180 --> 10:11.710
making it a place of healing.

10:14.260 --> 10:16.720
The water of that spring was delicious.

10:16.990 --> 10:18.250
I drank some, too.

10:18.250 --> 10:20.980
I wish you wouldn't use that
word given our situation.

10:20.980 --> 10:22.190
Sorry.

10:22.650 --> 10:24.090
It's a beautiful place,

10:24.090 --> 10:26.890
but not many people know about it,
so it's a deserted and quiet place.

10:27.160 --> 10:31.310
That's right. That's why I
made it my secret place.

10:31.490 --> 10:33.160
There was no one there?

10:33.160 --> 10:36.070
I remember playing with a little boy there.

10:36.290 --> 10:37.780
A boy?

10:37.780 --> 10:39.450
Yes, I think so...

10:39.930 --> 10:43.700
He pestered me to show him some
magic, and we played together.

10:43.980 --> 10:46.200
Now I remember.

10:46.670 --> 10:48.960
He pestered me, too,
so I made some fire.

10:49.330 --> 10:52.190
But he laughed and asked,
"That's all?" so I got mad.

10:52.190 --> 10:53.960
I wanted to forget about it, so I did.

10:54.280 --> 10:58.960
Oh, right. I accidentally
gouged the ruin's pillars.

10:58.960 --> 11:01.220
He glared at me coldly.

11:01.450 --> 11:05.290
There are people who can't treasure
historical cultural treasures.

11:05.290 --> 11:07.470
I couldn't help it.

11:07.780 --> 11:12.620
I was alone, so I had fun
playing with the boy.

11:12.980 --> 11:15.880
He told me it was a secret
we played together.

11:15.880 --> 11:20.280
He disappeared, and I haven't
told anyone about it until now.

11:20.640 --> 11:23.760
Now that I think of it,
he told me to come show him...

11:23.760 --> 11:25.710
...when I learned to use more than fire.

11:25.710 --> 11:27.230
Brings back memories.

11:27.230 --> 11:29.540
He told me to come back, too.

11:31.110 --> 11:35.470
Are the ruins at the spring the same
ones Leviatan saw in her dream?

11:37.220 --> 11:38.500
I don't know.

11:40.980 --> 11:45.120
But we won't find that spring in this desert.

11:45.120 --> 11:47.040
You're right.

11:47.040 --> 11:48.680
Maybe it's in a difference place.

11:48.990 --> 11:50.490
But what should we do?

11:50.490 --> 11:53.700
Should we continue searching aimlessly
in the desert like we did yesterday,

11:53.700 --> 11:57.190
or believe Leviatan's dream was
prophetic and look for the ruins?

11:57.480 --> 11:59.910
Shouldn't we search for the ruins?

11:59.910 --> 12:02.130
Well, let's say we're doing that.

12:02.130 --> 12:05.140
Are we going to keep walking without water?

12:05.140 --> 12:08.650
I want to take a shower, and I'd
at least like to wash my face.

12:08.650 --> 12:10.370
Just lick it.

12:10.610 --> 12:12.040
I'm not a cat!

12:12.360 --> 12:15.380
Why don't we at least decide
which direction we're going?

12:15.380 --> 12:17.200
We came this way yesterday.

12:17.200 --> 12:19.550
What should we do about the
other three directions?

12:19.840 --> 12:23.180
Let's go in the direction
this axe falls.

12:29.980 --> 12:30.890
This way.

12:33.650 --> 12:35.140
That's the way we came.

12:36.390 --> 12:38.570
We can't leave anything up to you.

12:44.670 --> 12:45.610
This way.

12:53.280 --> 12:53.870
There.

13:03.400 --> 13:04.400
Okay.

13:10.690 --> 13:14.280
Levi-tan, your dreams don't
contain many hints, do they?

13:14.280 --> 13:18.280
Sorry. I'll pay more attention next time.

13:18.280 --> 13:21.610
Please do. Think of how we feel.

13:21.950 --> 13:24.500
If we don't find your spear,

13:25.000 --> 13:26.660
maybe we'll have you
play a punishment game.

13:26.660 --> 13:28.700
What? A punishment game?

13:28.700 --> 13:30.400
What would be good?

13:30.400 --> 13:31.210
What?

13:31.210 --> 13:34.450
We should choose something so
embarrassing she'll blush.

13:34.450 --> 13:37.030
Leviatan always has a blank expression.

13:37.030 --> 13:37.960
That's good.

13:38.300 --> 13:41.510
Put positively, she's prim.
Put negatively, she's sulky.

13:42.540 --> 13:44.380
It's decided. You'll do a scale dance.

13:44.670 --> 13:49.150
We'll gather everyone in Haruna square and open Leviatan's scale dancing show.

13:49.150 --> 13:50.370
That's what we'll do.

13:51.590 --> 13:52.850
Are you okay?

13:52.850 --> 13:54.140
What happened?

13:54.140 --> 13:56.170
Ouch.

13:56.170 --> 13:58.960
Who put a pillar here?

13:58.960 --> 13:59.980
Talk about dangerous!

14:00.240 --> 14:01.070
A pillar?

14:04.610 --> 14:06.490
Hey, wait.

14:11.980 --> 14:13.580
Over there, everyone.

14:24.890 --> 14:26.440
There's water there!

14:26.440 --> 14:27.760
It's an oasis!

14:28.140 --> 14:29.650
All right!

14:48.420 --> 14:50.630
What? Where's the spring?

14:50.630 --> 14:51.700
It was right here, wasn't it?

14:52.050 --> 14:55.450
Why are we throwing sand
on each other and playing?

14:57.070 --> 14:58.210
This place...

15:01.810 --> 15:04.150
Is this the place you
saw in your dream?

15:04.150 --> 15:06.460
I don't know.

15:06.460 --> 15:09.150
In my dream, I was inside a building.

15:09.950 --> 15:12.320
Huh? What?

15:12.320 --> 15:13.900
This!

15:16.590 --> 15:17.970
Did you find something?

15:25.750 --> 15:26.930
It fits perfectly.

15:26.930 --> 15:30.110
Is this where the spring was?
You're kidding, right?

15:30.110 --> 15:33.940
But...it was a wonderful place
overflowing with water...

15:33.940 --> 15:36.330
I wonder when the spring dried up.

15:36.720 --> 15:38.880
Even the floating islands have fallen.

15:39.570 --> 15:43.880
I was looking forward to
coming back here, too.

15:43.880 --> 15:47.080
Why do I feel like a hole
has opened in my heart?

15:47.080 --> 15:47.720
Hey!

15:48.790 --> 15:50.280
It looks like we can go inside.

15:50.280 --> 15:54.370
I had no idea it was like
this when there was water.

15:57.710 --> 15:59.830
I think this is the place
I saw in my dream!

15:59.830 --> 16:01.520
What? Bingo?

16:05.110 --> 16:07.820
I remember seeing this
design in my dream.

16:07.820 --> 16:09.310
You're going?

16:09.310 --> 16:10.610
What are you talking about?

16:10.610 --> 16:12.780
We can't confirm if this is
the place if we don't go in.

16:12.780 --> 16:14.450
Yeah, but...

16:14.450 --> 16:15.620
Are you going to stay here?

16:16.020 --> 16:17.230
I'm going.

16:17.230 --> 16:18.010
Me, too.

16:18.010 --> 16:18.960
Yeah.

16:20.660 --> 16:22.240
Oh, really?!

16:22.240 --> 16:24.120
I'm staying right here!

16:26.050 --> 16:27.890
It's cool in here!

16:28.390 --> 16:30.820
It really is!

16:30.820 --> 16:32.630
It's so different from outside.

16:32.870 --> 16:34.550
What? Really?

16:35.560 --> 16:38.330
Maybe I'll go cool down a little bit.

16:38.330 --> 16:39.640
Just a little.

16:43.080 --> 16:45.910
This place is huge underground.

17:01.490 --> 17:02.790
Look! Over there!

17:09.280 --> 17:10.410
There it is.

17:10.980 --> 17:13.040
It's really here.

17:13.040 --> 17:15.300
You found it? Where?

17:15.300 --> 17:16.370
You're right.

17:16.370 --> 17:18.430
All right! That's great!

17:24.160 --> 17:25.370
What's wrong?

17:25.370 --> 17:30.020
This spear was stuck in
a monster in the ocean.

17:30.330 --> 17:33.370
But he said it was headed this way, right?

17:33.370 --> 17:36.420
Maybe it came all the way
here and dropped it.

17:36.420 --> 17:37.400
That can't be.

17:37.400 --> 17:39.870
This isn't a place you'd
happen to drop something.

17:39.870 --> 17:42.790
You're right. Could it be a trap?

17:43.070 --> 17:43.940
A trap?

17:44.620 --> 17:46.750
You're thinking about this too hard.

17:46.750 --> 17:47.880
I'll try pulling it out.

17:48.910 --> 17:50.260
Wait.

17:55.360 --> 17:58.920
Huh? I should be strong
enough to pull it out.

18:07.270 --> 18:09.280
That's weird.

18:10.160 --> 18:11.070
Mu-chan, you try.

18:11.360 --> 18:12.610
Me?

18:17.430 --> 18:21.370
There's no way I could pull
out something you couldn't.

18:21.660 --> 18:23.350
Levi-tan, it's your turn.

18:38.300 --> 18:39.460
It came out!

18:39.460 --> 18:40.640
You're kidding.

18:47.300 --> 18:50.040
I'm so glad to have my spear back.

18:51.510 --> 18:52.950
Levi-tan, behind you!

20:11.580 --> 20:19.350
Next Episode

20:14.500 --> 20:19.350
It's Definitely Suspicious!
